# Downloaded datasets (MNIST etc.) -- regenerate via whatever example
# script downloads them, don't commit the blobs. Root-anchored: unlike
# the MNIST/* rule above (which only matches a top-level MNIST/, not
# nested ones), this covers data/ wherever it sits at the repo root.
/data/

# Doxygen output -- regenerate with `doxygen Doxyfile`, don't commit it.
# docs/mainpage.md is hand-written Doxygen input and stays tracked.
